.TH SYSMONCTL 1 "2026" "sysmon 4.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sysmonctl \- query a running sysmond
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sysmonctl
.RB [ \-s
.IR socket ]
.RB [ \-w
.IR seconds ]
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sysmonctl
sends one command to
.BR sysmond (8)
over its unix socket and prints the reply. It exits with status 0 on
success, 1 when the daemon answers with an error, 2 on a usage error
and 3 when the daemon cannot be reached.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B ping
Check that the daemon is alive.
.TP
.BR list " [\fIpattern\fR]"
Metrics and their current values, optionally filtered with a shell glob.
.TP
.BI get " metric"
One value.
.TP
.BI history " metric" " \fR[\fIn\fR]"
The last
.I n
samples, oldest first.
.TP
.BI stats " metric" " \fR[\fIn\fR]"
Minimum, maximum, average, median and 95th percentile of the last
.I n
samples.
.TP
.B json
Every metric as a JSON object.
.TP
.B alerts
Alert rules and their state.
.TP
.B reload
Make the daemon re-read its configuration.
.TP
.BI wait " metric op value" " \fR[\fItimeout\fR]"
Poll every second until
.I metric op value
holds, with
.I op
one of > >= < <=. Exits 0 when it does, 4 after
.I timeout
seconds.
.TP
.BR top " [\fIseconds\fR]"
Full-screen dashboard. Keys: q quit, h help, space pause, / filter,
+ and \- change the refresh rate.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-s " socket"
Control socket. Defaults to
.B $SYSMON_SOCKET
or
.IR /tmp/sysmond.sock .
.TP
.BI \-w " seconds"
Repeat the command every
.I seconds
and redraw, like
.BR watch (1).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SYSMON_SOCKET
Default control socket.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colors in
.BR top .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sysmond (8)
